# cuts/v1.0.40/cut.env
# ============================================================================
# THE PINS FOR v1.0.40. Read by bin/rollforward_gate.sh --cut v1.0.40, by
# scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh, by scripts/resolve_cut_daemon_pin.sh,
# and by OS003 bin/cut.sh load_cut().
#
# THIS FILE IS THE AUTHORITATIVE HALF. OS003 carries a second cuts/v1.0.40/
# cut.env holding the operator's LOCAL PATHS. They are deliberately different
# documents. Do not merge them: vendoring OS003's copy here was tried and
# reverted because it carried operator working record, private box IPs and
# notarisation submission IDs into this PUBLIC repo.
#
# WHY v1.0.40 EXISTS: v1.0.39 SHIPS AN INSTALLER THAT MISREPORTS ITS VERSION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.39 is published, notarised, stapled and served at ostler.ai. Its
# payload is CORRECT -- measured on the published DMG, not on a build log:
#
#   both copies of install.sh in the artefact   a868054de321... = the v1.0.39 blob
#   OSTLER_ASSISTANT_VERSION default            0.4.61
#   ASSISTANT_FALLBACK_VERSION                  0.4.60   (correct by design)
#   Ostler.app + OstlerAssistant binaries       stamped bda4d7d8, zero 8ba3e948
#
# The single defect is that OstlerInstaller.app reports
# CFBundleShortVersionString 1.0.38 / CFBundleVersion 3800.
#
# THE MECHANISM, because "rebuilt it" is not a mechanism: gui/Makefile:120
# DERIVES the app version by READING gui/OstlerInstaller/Info.plist, and that
# plist was never bumped in the v1.0.39 tree. The build faithfully stamped the
# version the tagged tree asked for. Controlled: v1.0.36/37/38 each carried
# their own version, so v1.0.39 is the first break in four cuts.
#
# THE v1.0.39 TAG IS NOT BEING MOVED. It is published and a customer may
# already hold it; moving a published tag is worse than the defect it fixes.
#
# WHAT IS NEW IN THIS CUT BESIDES THE VERSION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   #955  the installer's own version must BE the version being cut, asserted
#         in cut.yml preflight against CUT_VERSION rather than against another
#         tracked file. Two gates already existed and neither could catch this:
#         installer-version-consistency.yml compares Info.plist, project.yml
#         and project.pbxproj TO EACH OTHER (all three said 1.0.38, so they
#         agreed), and OS003 #122 asserts the right thing but is an OPEN PR,
#         merged=never, so it has never run anywhere.
#   #957  the ARTEFACT's content must BE the tag being cut. Mounts the staged
#         DMG and hashes EVERY install.sh in it against the tag's blob, with
#         the nearest other v1.0.* tag as a runtime-resolved control. Raised by
#         TNM (#856, #844) after nothing in the cut had ever compared artefact
#         content to the tag -- the publish-integrity check proves only that
#         the DMG matches its OWN SHA256SUMS.
#         Publish is now gated on it: it carried `if: always()`, which would
#         have made the new gate report without blocking.
#
# THE DAEMON DOES NOT CHANGE. Still hub-v0.4.61 = bda4d7d8, already signed,
# notarised, stapled and published, with the hub app tarball beside it.
#
#     git rev-parse hub-v0.4.61^{}          bda4d7d837a086dc5008decfb1a7b5aeac616d68
#     install.sh DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TARBALL_SHA256 ff7b0b63...ced24, and that
#       digest was re-fetched anonymously from the published hub-v0.4.61
#       .sha256 sidecar and MATCHES.
# ============================================================================

CUT_VERSION=1.0.40

# The daemon. UNCHANGED from v1.0.39: hub-v0.4.61, signed, notarised, stapled.
DAEMON_COMMIT=bda4d7d837a0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE CM051 PIN. It must name the tree whose install.sh ships, compared BY BLOB.
#
# CARRIED OVER FROM v1.0.39 DELIBERATELY, AND MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED:
# install.sh has not changed since 8ecb383a, so the blob at that commit and the
# blob on the tree being cut are the same object.
#
#     git rev-parse 8ecb383a...:install.sh   25f09a220f73cc871cda7d4c9afc2d614df4a587
#     git rev-parse origin/main:install.sh   25f09a220f73cc871cda7d4c9afc2d614df4a587
#
# Nothing in this cut touches install.sh: the version bump is in the GUI
# plist/project files and the two new gates are tests plus workflow wiring.
# Confirm before the tag with:
#
#     bash scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh --ref origin/main
#
# v1.0.31 was burnt by a pin chosen early and trusted. Ancestry is not a
# defence: it proves ordering and says nothing about content.
CM051=8ecb383a8341d68736118c4b0518b2b6a9357ace
